<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Cleartext HTTP is blocked by default from targetSdk 28 up, which broke every
    app-side probe that used a plain-http URL: «Проверить соединение» defaults to
    NekoBox's http://cp.cloudflare.com/ and its HttpURLConnection threw
    "Cleartext HTTP traffic not permitted" on every tap, reported to the user as
    «Нет интернета» even through a perfectly healthy tunnel. The same applied to
    the GET/HEAD ping modes and to any http:// test URL a user types in.

    The core itself (Go) never consulted this policy, so the config's own urltest
    kept working — which is exactly why the failure looked like a UI bug.

    Same policy as the reference client (NekoBox's network_security_config.xml):
    a VPN client's probe/test endpoints are user-supplied and routinely plain
    http; refusing them in the platform layer only breaks diagnostics. Traffic
    that carries anything sensitive (subscription fetches) uses https on its own.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
